*.pickle

# 已弃用的实验分支（本地归档，不入库；确认不需要后可 rm -rf _archive）
_archive/

# rendered demo replays (mp4, ~21 MB) — regenerate with viz/replay_demos.py
viz/demo_replays/
*.mp4
# stray stderr captures from ad-hoc diagnostic runs
err_*.txt
exps/_stale/
cluster/ibrl.sif
*.sif
.pylibs/
plots/
release/data
real2sim/splats

# The real ZED captures used for the real2sim calibration are committed as
# LOSSLESS PNG (byte-identical copies of the originals) -- *.png above is a
# plotting-bloat rule, and these are calibration INPUTS, not plots. JPEG was
# measured to move the external-camera PnP solution by 2.3 mm mean / 4.3 mm max,
# which is the same order as the whole grounding chain's 6.1 mm, so lossy copies
# would not reproduce the published numbers.
!real2sim/zed_capture/**/*.png
!real2sim/zed_capture/*.png

# real2sim render comparisons (PNG, and PNG on purpose -- these are evidence for
# measured claims in docs/real2sim.md, not plots). `superseded_*` stays ignored:
# those were made with the wrong ZED intrinsics / the exposure-comp splat and
# must not be quoted.
!viz/splat_before_after/*.png
!viz/peg_on_real_table/*.png
!viz/zedview_check/*.png
!viz/wrist_handeye/*.png
viz/splat_before_after/superseded_*
# wrist hand-eye: superseded_* were made with the WRONG sim gripper (Robotiq85,
# while scan_run2 has a Panda hand) or are the circular per-pose-PnP splat check
# that tests the board model rather than T_ee_zedm.  DISPUTED_* assert the robot
# had no gripper in scan_run2, which is false (see 11_PROOF_...).  None quotable.
viz/wrist_handeye/superseded_*
viz/wrist_handeye/DISPUTED_*
# peg object/scene splats. superseded_* = made before the crop used colour (which
# is what separates a flat board from a flat patch of table) or before the scene
# double-transform was found. Not quotable.
!viz/objsplats/*.png
viz/objsplats/superseded_*
